<http://data.silknow.org/object/d88c079f-2e85-35ec-8cd3-c60c23e1c6ef/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven silk and metal thread.\nTwo pieces seamed horizontally have been added down the left hand side. Striped pattern:\n[1] light blue ground with a red flower and a pair of green leaves offset with two half motifs. [2] wider strip with a gold ground [silver strip close S-wound on a yellow silk core bound with pink silk warp] and a large floral spray. There is a pair of green leaves, a pair of red tulips [or are they lilies?] and then a central red flower surrounded by green leaves. [3] as [1].\n[4] undecorated gold stripe.\nThere is a woven inscription across the top of the main piece."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d88c079f-2e85-35ec-8cd3-c60c23e1c6ef> .

